### Section 7 — Learn App Progress Tracking ✅ 10/10

| # | Test | Status | Detail |
|---|------|--------|--------|
| T48 | Learn page has `IS_AUTHENTICATED` JS var | ✅ PASS | — |
| T49 | Save progress API returns 200 | ✅ PASS | HTTP 200 |
| T50 | Save progress returns correct counts | ✅ PASS | mastered=3, guided=5 |
| T51 | Progress persisted in DB | ✅ PASS | mastered=3, guided(only)=2 |
| T52 | Load progress API returns 200 | ✅ PASS | — |
| T53 | Load progress returns correct letters | ✅ PASS | mastered=['A', 'B', 'C'] |
| T54 | Load progress returns guided letters | ✅ PASS | guided=['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E'] |
| T55 | Save progress rejected for anon (401) | ✅ PASS | HTTP 401 |
| T56 | Load progress returns empty for anon | ✅ PASS | `{mastered: [], guided: []}` |
| T57 | UserProfile.total_signs_practiced updated | ✅ PASS | total_signs_practiced=8 |

> [!TIP]
> **Dual-storage architecture works correctly:**
> - **Logged-in users:** Progress syncs to both `localStorage` AND the PostgreSQL database via the `/learn/api/save-progress/` API
> - **Anonymous users:** Progress is saved to `localStorage` only (API returns 401 for save attempts)
> - **Cross-device persistence:** When a logged-in user opens the Learn page, server-saved progress loads first, overriding any stale localStorage data
> - **Stats integration:** `UserProfile.total_signs_practiced` is automatically updated when progress is saved

